        "id": 1529242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-11T17:41:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assume that this is because the MPU only protects internal storage so if `CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` then MPU isn\u0027t protecting RO flash. Right? If so, it\u0027s probably worth adding a comment.\n\nAs a side note, is it possible for the MPU to protect the aliased SPI flash addresses?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 142,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "226997e6b4ac716863a8d85893053c6994841f4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55d1bc18_8155648d",
        "filename": "test/mpu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1551272
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-11T22:15:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The inclusion of both of these checks is based entirely on\nsrc/platform/ec/core/cortex-m/mpu.c\n\nwhere\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE) || !defined(CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL)\"\nmpu_protect_code_ram()\n#else\nmpu_lock_ro_flash()\nmpu_lock_get_rw_regions()\nmpu_lock_rw_flash()\n#endif\n\nThere is also precedent in the existing test/mpu.c around mpu_protect_code_ram() where the opposite #if is used to enable the test.\nMy understanding is that the ARM based MPU is flexible enough to protect any memory address including aliased SPI flash addresses. We should likely confirm with Nuvoton.",
      "parentUuid": "efc06feb_464f5385",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 142,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "226997e6b4ac716863a8d85893053c6994841f4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
